    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Act as a Polyglot Language Tutor teaching English, Kannada, Japanese, and Korean. Choose one high-frequency 'everyday' word.\n\nExcluded Words (words chosen previously):\n- English: {{ $json.concatenated_English }}\n- Kannada: {{ $json.concatenated_Kannada }}\n- Japanese: {{ $json.concatenated_Japanese }}\n- Korean: {{ $json.concatenated_Korean }}\n\nFor each language (EN, KN, JP, KR), provide:\n- Word & Phonetics: Script + [Romaji/IAST]. \n- Etymology: A brief origin story to aid memory.\n- The Sentence: One natural sentence at a Standard Polite level. Align the Kannada, Korean, and Japanese versions to demonstrate their SOV similarity.\n-Cultural Note: Highlight any nuances in usage or social context.\n\nLanguage-specific instructions:\n- For Korean and Japanese, if the word is a hanja/kanji, give other examples of where it's used\n- For Korean, include hanja if applicable\n- For Kannada, if the word is a prefix or suffix of another word, give examples\n- For Kannada, avoid textbook Kannada and use colloquial Kannada\n- For Japanese, all kanji must have hiragana written next to it in parentheses\n- For Kannada, all scripts must have english written next to it in parentheses\n",
        "needsFallback": true
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [320, 112],
      "id": "ai-agent-tutor",
      "name": "AI Agent"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b",
        "options": {
          "temperature": 1
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGroq",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [336, 336],
      "id": "groq-model-primary",
